# Tests

xUnit. Name tests `Method_Scenario_ExpectedResult`.

Test behaviour, not implementation. A test that restates the code it covers
catches nothing and blocks refactoring.

Every issue needs the happy path plus at least two edge cases. The edges that
actually matter in this project:

- empty bag; drawing more tiles than the bag holds
- reshuffle triggered mid-draw when the draw pile empties
- a word reusing a single tile twice
- a word longer than the hand; zero-length input
- removing the last copy of a letter from the bag

Seeded behaviour must assert *reproducibility*, not plausibility: run the same
seed twice and assert the sequences are equal. Never assert on a specific
shuffled order produced by the current implementation, because that couples the
test to the RNG algorithm rather than to determinism.

Use real instances over mocks. `IRandomSource` and `IWordSource` exist so tests
can pass simple fakes; nothing else needs an interface.
